# Cloudflare Pages header rules for the public Phoenix build (PRD #855).
#
# Copied to `dist/_headers` by .github/workflows/deploy-demo.yml. Pages reads it
# from the root of the uploaded directory; GitHub Pages (the dev host, ci.yml)
# ignores it entirely, which is why the dev site's caching is not this file's
# business.
#
# Asserted by `scripts/check-deploy-headers.mjs` against a deployed URL, and by
# `tests/client/deploy-headers.test.js` against canned fixtures. The same
# contract is served by the native host (`src/delivery/http.rs`); two
# implementations, one contract.
#
# ── The rule about rules ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# NO TWO PATTERNS HERE MAY SET THE SAME HEADER. Pages applies every matching
# rule, and this repository has no way to test which one wins when two set
# `Cache-Control` — so the file is written to make the question not arise. That
# is why `/*` carries only security headers, and why the media directories are
# listed one by one instead of as `/assets/*` (which would overlap
# `/assets/scenarios.toml`, the one asset under there that must never be held).
#
# Everything not named below keeps Pages' own default — `public, max-age=0,
# must-revalidate`. That is already correct for the two entry points and for the
# scenario manifest, and merely conservative (a 304 round-trip) for anything
# else, so silence here is safe in a way an over-broad rule would not be.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# The content-addressed bundle: `project-phoenix-<hash>.js` and
# `project-phoenix-<hash>_bg.wasm` (`.wasm.gz` on the demo, which ships the
# binary gzipped under the Pages 25 MiB file cap and decompresses it in the
# page). The filename changes when the bytes do, which would licence caching it
# for a year — deliberately capped at 4 hours instead, matching the dashboard
# Cache Rule already in force for this zone, at the cost of a revalidation
# round-trip on any return visit past the window. It is still the single
# largest download on the site, so most of the caching win still lands here.
#
# Deliberately NOT `/*.js`: `dist/phoenix.js` (scripts/wasm-editor-alias.mjs) is
# a STABLE name re-exporting the hashed glue, and `gui/*.js` are copied
# verbatim. Caching either for 4 hours the way the hashed bundle is would still
# strand a deploy for up to that long.
/project-phoenix-*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate

# Pages' own extension-based default for `.js` is `application/javascript`, which
# does not match `text/javascript; charset=utf-8` from `content_type_for` in
# `src/delivery/http.rs` — the native host and Pages must agree, so it is pinned
# here rather than left to Pages' default. The `.wasm.gz` sibling under
# `/project-phoenix-*` needs no such override: Pages' own `.gz` default of
# `application/gzip` already matches the contract.
/project-phoenix-*.js
  Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8

# Media: stable within a deploy, not content-addressed, so an hour — long enough
# to spare a returning player the round-trips, short enough that a deploy is
# live within one.
/assets/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/assets/skybox/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/assets/planets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/assets/sounds/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
